# Export fixtures are BYTE-EXACT test expectations: CSV is CRLF-terminated with
# a UTF-8 BOM, JSON is LF-terminated. This repo is developed on Windows with
# core.autocrlf=true, which would rewrite both on checkout and break the
# fixture comparison tests on a fresh clone. Take these files literally.
src/lib/export/fixtures/** -text

# Import fixtures are byte-exact INPUTS: the RB fixture reproduces that
# format's real quirks, which include CRLF endings and a final row with no
# trailing newline. autocrlf=true would rewrite them and quietly destroy the
# two traps they exist to catch. Scoped to *.csv so the JSON fixture, which is
# already normalised in the index, is left alone.
src/lib/import/fixtures/*.csv -text
